WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.251
In real processes several quantities influence each other: the temperatures of two rooms,

2
00:00:07.251 --> 00:00:12.629
numbers of predators and prey, susceptible and infected computers.

3
00:00:12.629 --> 00:00:19.310
In this lesson we write such systems in matrix form and solve them by elimination.

4
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:26.749
In a normal system the derivative of each unknown is expressed through the others.

5
00:00:26.749 --> 00:00:35.427
In the linear case we collect the coefficients into a matrix A and write X prime equals A X plus F.

6
00:00:35.427 --> 00:00:43.142
An n-th order equation also becomes a system: take y, y prime and so on as new unknowns.

7
00:00:43.392 --> 00:00:50.518
Example: x prime equals two x plus y, y prime equals three x plus four y.

8
00:00:50.518 --> 00:00:55.790
From the first equation, y equals x prime minus two x.

9
00:00:55.790 --> 00:01:03.014
Differentiate the first equation and replace y prime using the second one.

10
00:01:03.264 --> 00:01:10.093
This gives x double prime minus six x prime plus five x equals zero.

11
00:01:10.093 --> 00:01:14.310
The characteristic roots are one and five.

12
00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:19.934
So x equals C one e to the t plus C two e to the five t.

13
00:01:20.184 --> 00:01:32.581
We do not integrate for y; we substitute into y equals x prime minus two x: y equals minus C one e to the t plus three C two e to the five t.

14
00:01:32.581 --> 00:01:39.614
No extra constant appears: a system with two unknowns has exactly two constants.

15
00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:48.875
With x of zero equal to one and y of zero equal to seven we get C one minus one and C two equal to two.

16
00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:57.974
The graph shows x and y in time: both grow fast, like e to the five t, because the largest root is five.

17
00:01:58.224 --> 00:02:07.060
Question: how many first-order equations do we get when reducing a third-order equation to a normal system?

18
00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.032
Pause the video, choose your answer,

19
00:02:10.032 --> 00:02:16.886
then read the explanation and go back to the relevant part of the lesson if needed.
